  "note": "Triennial town commissioners election of May 1949. No newspaper report has been found; the Belfast and Ulster Directory 1950 lists the nine commissioners. Nine commissioners printed (chairman Cecil M'Ilroy, probably the Cecil M'Elroy of 1946). Robert Leckey is printed both as a commissioner and as clerk. Directory list, not an election report: the directory prints the council's membership as it stood when the edition was compiled (late in the year after the election). It does not say whether members were returned at a poll or unopposed, and cannot show co-options made between the election and compilation. No votes."
